A||N||5||turbo86se||Is this safe?||||1||
Z||000000||turbo86se||07-28-2001||12:21 PM||||A few days ago while cleaning up the SE for Williamsburg, I removed the decklid deadbolt locking system that has never worked in my 86SE. It had a small module that attached to the drivers side of the glove box, through the firewall. Now I have a 1" hole directly behind my head. Kinda cool cause I can really hear the turbo spool up   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I'm worried about gases and such. What could I plug it with? Temporarily I've stuck a small piece of cloth in there. But what else could I do?<BR>TIA!!<P>Oh yeah, I don't have any exhaust leaks.<p>[This message has been edited by turbo86se (edited 07-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||07-28-2001||12:27 PM||||You may not have exhaust leaks now but you don't want to find out when you do get a crack by passing out. Especially with a turbo set up.  There are many ways of sealing up the hole but probably one of the cheapest a piece of sheet metal and some rtv sealant.||||reg||6
Z||000002||theogre||07-28-2001||01:15 PM||||I'd use metal and epoxy. much tougher than RTV Silicone. Clean the metals good and rough them up a bit for the best bond. Paint it to keep it from rusting and to hide it if it shows. (Paint will stick to the epoxy fine but not RTV.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||07-28-2001||01:47 PM||||Great! Thanks for the tips guys. I appreciate it. I figured I could block it somehow, now I just hope nobody noticed the hole inside the car during judging at Williamsburg. <P>Oh well, I'm just there to have fun, meet some great people, and the feeling of everywhere I turn more Fieros!! YEAH!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||07-28-2001||04:02 PM||||You might try going to one of the local commercial two-way radio shops, where they fix taxi-cab and cop-car radios. Many of those radios use antennas that mount in a 3/4" hole drilled into the body. When they are removed, they place a rubber plug into the hole. If you go in and ask, they'll probably just give you one, or sell you one at a nominal fee. Seal it in with some silicone.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||07-29-2001||12:25 AM||||A wilkey button. It is a spring steel snap in plug used in electrical boxes. They are about 20 cents at most hardware stores.||||reg||1
